/**
 * Stories from Ferdowsi's Shahnameh, retold in our own words for children of different ages, with `saga` set so a family can
 * read them in the poem's own order. Those already told elsewhere (Hushang, Jamshid, Kaveh, Zal and the Simorgh, Rostam and
 * Rakhsh, Kavus's flying throne, Gordafarid) carry the same `saga` in their own files.
 *
 * `lang: 'fa'`: told in the Persian app only. The Persian in src/i18n/locales/fa/stories-shahnameh.json is what a parent
 * reads aloud, and the English here is a faithful rendering of it. Every plot was read in the poem itself, through Ganjoor,
 * and every change made for children is named in the record's `note`. The research, with couplet numbers, what was cut and
 * why, and the episodes left out on purpose (Forud, the death of Siavash, the death of Rostam, Lonbak and Baraham, Azadeh), is
 * in research_notes/PlayNest phase 11 research round 8, notes 01 to 03. Rostam and Sohrab is told for 11 and 12 only, read with a
 * parent, by the owner's decision; its note names everything left out, including Rostam's attempt on his own life.
 *
 * Order numbers follow the poem: 1 the poet, 10–60 the first kings, 60–100 Fereydun to Rostam's youth, 100–200 the heroes,
 * 200 and on the later kings.
 */
