    note: "From Ferdowsi's Shahnameh. Ferdowsi says a div is 'a bad person who does not give thanks', so the story is about thinking before you answer someone who wants to trick you. In the poem Rostam also fights the king of Turan's herdsmen, and he kills Akvan with his mace and sword; here he simply finds Rakhsh grazing and beats the div. A great stone called Akvan's stone turns up again in the story of Bizhan.",
