    paragraphs: [
      'Bizhan, son of Giv, was a young hero of Iran. Once, after he had driven off the wild boars that were ruining the farmers’ fields, his jealous companion Gorgin led him on into Turan, where he should not have gone, and then went home without him.',
      'In Turan, Bizhan and Manizheh, the daughter of King Afrasiab, became the closest of friends. But her father was furious that she had befriended a hero from Iran. He had Bizhan chained in a deep, dark pit, covered with a huge stone, Akvan’s stone, that elephants had to drag there. And he was angry with Manizheh too, and sent her out of the palace with nothing.',
      'But Manizheh did not leave her friend. Every morning she went from door to door asking for bread, and she passed it down to Bizhan through a gap beside the stone.',
      'In Iran, King Kay Khosrow looked into his cup that shows the whole world, and saw Bizhan in the pit. He called for Rostam. Rostam and seven heroes dressed up as merchants and came with a caravan of camels to the city of Khotan, where Rostam opened a jewel shop.',
      "Manizheh heard that a merchant had come from Iran, and ran to him in tears. 'Bizhan lies in a pit here, in chains! Tell the heroes of Iran!' Rostam was afraid someone might find him out, so he spoke roughly: 'Go away! I know nothing of them.' Manizheh wept. 'Is this the way of Iran, not to answer someone in need?'",
      "Then Rostam's heart softened. He had his cook bring her a hot roast bird wrapped in soft bread. And quick as a fairy, Rostam slipped his ring inside it. 'Take this to the pit,' he said.",
      'Manizheh ran to the pit and passed the bread down. Bizhan unwrapped it, and there was the ring. It had a turquoise seal, with a name cut into it, fine as a hair: Rostam. Bizhan laughed out loud, so loud that it rang out of the pit.',
      "'Help has come,' he told Manizheh. 'Go to the merchant and whisper: are you the lord of Rakhsh?' She ran like the wind. 'Yes,' said Rostam. 'I have come all this way for him. Gather wood by day, and at night light a fire as big as a mountain, so that I can find the pit.'",
      'All day Manizheh gathered wood, and when it was dark she lit a great fire. Rostam saw it and rode there with his seven heroes. They pushed at the stone, but it did not move. Then Rostam asked God for strength, lifted the stone and threw it far into the forest. The ground shook.',
      "'When I heard your voice,' Bizhan called up, 'all the bitterness in the world turned sweet.' 'I have one wish,' said Rostam. 'Forgive Gorgin, who did this to you. Put the anger out of your heart.' 'You don't know what he did to me!' cried Bizhan. 'If you will not listen to me,' said Rostam, 'I will leave you here and ride home.' Bizhan was quiet. Then he said, 'Gorgin did me wrong. But I forgive him. My heart is at rest.'",
      'Rostam let down his lasso and pulled Bizhan up, thin and pale and heavy with chains, and broke the chains with his own hands. Gorgin, who was one of the seven heroes, bowed to the ground and said he was sorry, and Bizhan forgave him and did not pay him back. Then Bizhan and Manizheh set off together for Iran, safe at last.',
    ],
